KZ3 patch 1132 (SPU pass 111; upstream candidate): vector forms for the SPU helpers GCC compiled badly, under
__SSE4_1__ (the loops stay for other builds).
- mpy, mpya, mpys, mpyi, mpyh, mpyhh, mpyhha (signed 16 x 16) as pmaddwd with the other halfword of one operand
  zeroed; mpyu, mpyui, mpyhhu, mpyhhau (unsigned) as pmulld on zero-extended halves. GCC vectorized the loops through a
  pshufb gather of the even halfwords, two sign extensions and two pmulld on half vectors; spu_mpya alone was 4.6 % of
  the K4 SPU samples (SPU pass 111 profile, runs spu-r110-p*b).
- clz: per-lane bsr loop (four lane stores, then a 16-byte reload = a failed store-to-load forward) replaced by the
  float-exponent form on x & ~(x >> 1) (cannot round up to the next power of two).
- cntb (nibble pshufb table), gb/gbh/gbb (movemask), fsm/fsmh (compare against bit masks).
- and, or, xor, nand, nor, andc, orc, selb as pand/por/pxor/pandn: on the two _u64 halves GCC sometimes computed them
  in general registers and stored 2 x 8 bytes that the next op read back as 16 (failed store forward).
Same bits as the loops: tools/spu/test_r111_vec.sh (mpy/mpyu on every 16-bit pair, clz on every input, the rest on
16 M random vectors plus edges; negative controls), built -msse4.1 -mfma, + -mavx2 and -mno-sse4.1.

